{
  "id": 216362805,
  "iid": 10250,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "dhcpv4: Fix DHCP Option 124 parsing",
  "description": "Takes a stab at addressing #18970 which shows how DHCP Option 124 is being parsed incorrectly. Please see that issue for more details.\n\nThis MR updates the field labels to be non-cablelabs specific, and adds a new subtree to hold each individual vendor-class-data-item.\n\nI would love a little help, or a nudge in the right direction of best-practices for doing better bounds checking when dissecting individual options. Also this code adds a new subtree and set of fields to dhcp for the parsing of this option and I am not confident if this was done correctly or completely.\n\n\n### Sample tshark output (only showing the option in question)\n\nSample pcap: [dhcp-option-124-correct.pcapng](/uploads/3ae052a3c01f82ca92a5ca18493f9424/dhcp-option-124-correct.pcapng)\n\n\n```console\n# tshark -r /pcaps/dhcp-option-124-correct.pcap -V\n\n   Option: (124) V-I Vendor Class\n        Length: 19\n        Enterprise: Broadband Forum (3561)\n            Length: 14\n            Vendor Class Data Item\n                Length: 4\n                Data: 63776d70\n            Vendor Class Data Item\n                Length: 4\n                Data: 74657374\n            Vendor Class Data Item\n                Length: 3\n                Data: 757370\n\n```",
  "state": "merged",
