    {
      "id": "0341d936ff37db92a40fff5b9dcc3ce788022065",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1347088166,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Thanks @alagoutte, can you please teach me a little more about how this should work? I was essentially trying to copy how the earlier length field `hf_dhcp_option_vi_class_data_length` is parsed:\n\n```c\nproto_tree_add_item(tree, hf_dhcp_option_vi_class_data_length, tvb, offset, 1, ENC_BIG_ENDIAN);\n```\n\nand later registered:\n```c\n{ &hf_dhcp_option_vi_class_data_length,\n  { \"Length\", \"dhcp.option.vi_class.length\",\n    FT_UINT8, BASE_DEC, NULL, 0x0,\n    \"Option 124: Length\", HFILL }},\n```\n\nI thought I was doing the same thing with the `hf_dhcp_option_vi_class_data_item_length` and `hf_dhcp_option_vi_class_data_item_data`. I've pushed a new commit to use `ENC_NA` within the proto_tree_add_item call, but am not entirely sure if that's correct, or why the difference.\n\nThank you!",
          "author": {
            "id": 4502906,
            "username": "zachad",
            "public_email": "zachad@qacafe.com",
            "name": "Zach Chadwick",
            "state": "active",
